---
args: {"docket": "DepartureDocket", "portfolio": "HandoverPortfolio | null"}
returns: "ContinuityPlan"
---
1. Bind prior = portfolio when supplied, otherwise an empty HandoverPortfolio at revision zero with empty promise, progress, prerequisite, slice, introduction and reply arrays, and CaptureBoundary { accessibleSourceIds: [], frozenSourceIds: [], selectiveSharingRequests: [], unavailableSourceIds: [], captureReceiptIds: [], accessState: "unresolved" }. Bind capture = determineAccessCapture(docket). When access is revoked, use only previously authorized frozen source snapshots and their actual capture receipts. Request selective sharing of a relevant personal note; do not recover revoked mail or export a notebook.
2. Bind promises = reconstructPromiseEpisodes(docket, capture). Preserve the historical promisor and unknown due dates. Bind progress = matchOutcomeAcceptance(promises, docket.correspondence). A due date passing or a file being sent does not satisfy an acceptance condition.
3. For promises with open, partial or uncertain work bind prerequisites = discoverContinuityPrerequisites(promises, progress, docket). Detect cycles through the finite dependency identities; retain unresolved owners and minimal recovery tasks. Completed/cancelled promises do not acquire fabricated access tasks.
4. Bind slices = offerSuccessorSlices(promises, progress, prerequisites, docket, portfolio). Preserve every earlier exact scope acknowledgment; split a partially accepted project into accepted and unowned portions before counting transferred responsibility. A recurring obligation's proposed cadence remains unconfirmed until owner evidence supports it.
5. Bind introductions = prepareCustomerIntroductions(promises, slices, docket, portfolio). Keep reviewed wording, actual dispatch and receipt separately; an expected named contact needs a consented introduction, not a silent reassignment.
6. Bind closure = reviewImmediateContinuity(promises, progress, prerequisites, slices, introductions). Bind nextPortfolio: HandoverPortfolio = { revision: advance only when a new source, progress finding, prerequisite, accepted-scope change, introduction receipt or capture boundary was established; otherwise preserve prior.revision, promises: merge by stable promise key while retaining historical source IDs and never inventing due dates, progress: merge by promise key using only delivery/acceptance evidence while preserving remaining scope, prerequisites: retain unresolved prior dependencies and append only currently supported recovery tasks, slices: preserve every exact prior acceptance revision and append newly accepted or unowned scope from slices, introductions: retain prior delivery receipts and append only reviewed current intents or actual matching receipts from introductions, capture: current supported capture boundary, replyIds: prior replyIds plus unique source reply identities actually present in docket.correspondence }. Do not convert a proposed successor, cadence or introduction into acceptance. Return { portfolio: nextPortfolio, openWork: closure.openWork, unacceptedTransfers: closure.unacceptedTransfers, missingAccess: closure.missingAccess, cycles: closure.cycles, transferComplete: closure.transferComplete, workComplete: closure.workComplete, questions: closure.questions }. Transfer closure requires every immediate obligation to have an accepting owner and confirmed next checkpoint even when delivery work remains open.
